1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,670
♪

2
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,380
[COCO] Is an athlete
an athlete

3
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:09,130
from the moment they're born?

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:13,470
What about astronauts,
or pop stars?

5
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:17,690
You don't know what you'll be
until you've grown up.

6
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:21,610
So, is it the same for witches?

7
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:28,860
[footsteps]

8
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:47,460
[Coco sighs]

9
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:49,130
[wind blowing]

10
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,550
[Coco exclaims]

11
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,460
[sighs tiredly]

12
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:23,630
Oh! I'm making
a big mess, aren't I?

13
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:25,710
Sorry, I'm almost done.

14
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:31,130
Don't worry,
it'll go back to normal.

15
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:34,390
This spring is touched
by magic!

16
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:00,660
I'll never get tired of it.

17
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,750
Magic is so... amazing!

18
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:10,510
The world around us
is brimming with magic.

19
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:14,510
A blessing that improves
our lives in so many ways.

20
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,140
THE MAGIC
THAT STARTED EVERYTHING

21
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:18,720
But how it works
is a bit of a mystery.

22
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:22,270
The only ones who can
cast spells are witches.

23
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:23,850
[cattle bleating]

24
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:27,270
[COCO] All we ordinary people
can do is sit back

25
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:29,520
and enjoy the results.

26
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:32,360
But we can never use
magic ourselves.

27
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:37,240
I wish I had been born a witch.

28
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:41,620
Hm?

29
00:02:45,210 --> 00:02:47,170
Oh, sheets of white,

30
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:50,380
become now a cloak of flight!

31
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,340
Uh...

32
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,180
[gasps] No, come back!

33
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,720
This isn't the kind
of flight I meant!

34
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:03,270
[gasps]

35
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:04,940
♪

36
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,190
[exclaims softly]

37
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:14,490
[Coco panting]

38
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,990
A Pegasus Carriage!

39
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:20,200
♪

40
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,830
[exclaims excitedly]

41
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:33,510
I've never seen one land!
I can't wait!

42
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,300
Mom, look!

43
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:39,010
There's a Pegasus Carriage!

44
00:03:39,050 --> 00:03:40,430
Mom!

45
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,770
Mom, where are you?

46
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:45,680
Mom?

47
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,810
Oh...

48
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,270
[BOTH] Huh?

49
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:52,440
[QIFREY] Hm.

50
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,690
I'm sorry, sir!
I didn't know you were there.

51
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,240
It's quite all right.

52
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:58,570
It was my own fault.
A poor place to stand.

53
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:00,530
[WOMAN 1]
My word, I can't believe it!

54
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:03,280
Imagine, finding such a garment
all the way out here!

55
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:06,120
[WOMAN 2] Ah, yes, but isn't
wood-sorrel embroidery

56
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,120
a tad dated?

57
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,580
Oh, look at this!

58
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:10,790
-Genuine Harrian lace!
-[both gasp]

59
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,750
[WOMAN 2] Amazing! The stock
in the castle town

60
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:15,170
-sold out almost immediately.
-[Coco exclaims]

61
00:04:15,210 --> 00:04:16,670
-[indistinct chatter]
-It must have been them!

62
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,090
They came
in the Pegasus Carriage!

63
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:21,970
-[women chuckle]
-Oh. No, I'm not with them.

64
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:25,310
Pardon me, but do you perhaps
have any more lace like this?

65
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:26,390
[COCO'S MOM]
Oh, of course, ma'am.

66
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:28,310
I'll be right with you!

67
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:30,650
Coco? I could use your help!

68
00:04:30,690 --> 00:04:32,110
[WOMAN 3] How about this one?

69
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,690
What can we do for you, sir?

70
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:36,110
I was looking for some
smoke-colored fabric.

71
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,610
But I can come again.

72
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:39,450
I could cut it for you
if you like!

73
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:40,700
Will you, now?

74
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,490
You're in good hands with her!

75
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:44,080
-I see.
-[indistinct chatter continues]

76
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,700
[gasps excitedly]
When I'm done,

77
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:49,620
can I go see
the Pegasus Carriage?

78
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,040
Go see the what?

79
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,130
There's a Pegasus Carriage
outside!

80
00:04:53,170 --> 00:04:54,420
Oh, for goodness' sake.

81
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,710
We've talked about this.

82
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:57,630
No meddling
with the customers' property.

83
00:04:57,670 --> 00:04:59,300
[COCO] I'll only look,
I promise!

84
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:00,880
[Coco's mom sighs]

85
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:02,590
[COCO] I'll stop talking about

86
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:05,890
how I want to be a witch
all the time. Please?

87
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:06,970
[COCO'S MOM] Mm...

88
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:08,850
-[indistinct chatter continues]
-[Coco's mom sighs]

89
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:11,350
All right, fine, but
only after you've finished.

90
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:13,440
[gasps excitedly] Thank you.

91
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:17,110
Sorry to keep you waiting!
What measurements did you need?

92
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,860
-[QIFREY] Oh, here they are.
-I'll be right back.

93
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:21,530
♪

94
00:05:33,790 --> 00:05:35,710
[inhales, blows softly]

95
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:37,130
♪

96
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,680
[sighs]

97
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,850
[COCO] Uh?

98
00:05:57,570 --> 00:05:59,650
[Coco whimpers]

99
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:00,860
My...

100
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,950
You have excellent focus
and steady hands.

101
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:08,740
No hesitation in the line.
Clean cut.

102
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:11,660
And a finish showing
precision and care.

103
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,920
I had no idea
this village possessed

104
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,540
such a skilled artisan.

105
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:18,460
This is real magic.

106
00:06:18,710 --> 00:06:19,840
[Coco gasps]

107
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:24,260
[shrieks] No! What I do here
isn't anything like magic!

108
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,220
Magic is mysterious,
and priceless,

109
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,970
and wonderfully shiny
and sparkly,

110
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:29,970
and unbelievably beautiful!

111
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:34,060
It's just so... so precious,

112
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:36,400
more precious than I can say.

113
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,570
Actually, come to think of it,
what am I saying?

114
00:06:39,610 --> 00:06:42,070
I'm getting the sense
you truly love magic.

115
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:46,570
Why is that? Tell me.

116
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:48,620
[Coco sighs]

117
00:06:51,910 --> 00:06:54,250
[COCO] When I was little,
my mother took me

118
00:06:54,290 --> 00:06:56,420
to a festival at the castle.

119
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,880
And while I was there,

120
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,500
I met a witch wearing a mask.

121
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:02,170
[♪ mysterious music playing]

122
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,770
[WITCH] You there, child.

123
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:22,980
Would you like to buy
a magic picture book?

124
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,530
Magic?

125
00:07:27,570 --> 00:07:29,030
I love picture books,

126
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:31,410
but I've never heard of magic.

127
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:36,420
[WITCH] Why, magic is a miracle
that makes this world vibrant.

128
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:39,130
A Pegasus Carriage in the sky,

129
00:07:39,170 --> 00:07:42,420
a spring with waters
ever crystal clear.

130
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,170
Even the cobblestones underfoot,

131
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,930
glowing brightly with each step.

132
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:50,680
All of these things are magic.

133
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,850
[gasps delightedly]

134
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:54,600
So pretty!

135
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,850
Wow, magic is the best!

136
00:07:56,890 --> 00:07:58,650
Thank you, I love magic!

137
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:01,270
[WITCH] Buy the book
and get this wand for free.

138
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,690
♪

139
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,530
Really? That's what you spent
the money on?

140
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,620
I thought you wanted to get
some roasted strawberries.

141
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,910
I did! But then
I followed a butterfly,

142
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:15,120
and I found a person
wearing a pointed hat!

143
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,410
Yes, so you told me
once already.

144
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:20,170
And now, I have
a magic picture book!

145
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:21,580
And a wand too!

146
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,040
[Coco's mom chuckles]

147
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,960
All right, then.
It's getting late, Coco,

148
00:08:26,010 --> 00:08:27,420
we should start heading home.

149
00:08:27,470 --> 00:08:29,130
-[COCO] Mommy!
-Hm?

150
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,430
When I grow up,

151
00:08:30,470 --> 00:08:32,600
I'm going to become a witch
and use my magic

152
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:34,850
to make the whole world vibrant,
just you wait!

153
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:36,430
You can't.

154
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,020
But why not?

155
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:42,810
Darling, you can't simply decide
to become a witch and use magic.

156
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:45,730
It's a power
you have to be born with.

157
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:48,360
Unfortunately, it's not
something ordinary people

158
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,740
are capable of.

159
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,530
Now, if you're ready,
let's go home.

160
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:57,330
But look! The ground shines
wherever I step!

161
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,370
[COCO'S MOM] Uh...

162
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,460
[both chuckle]

163
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,380
[COCO'S MOM] Well, let's see
if it keeps on shining

164
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:05,130
all the way home.

165
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:08,420
If so, maybe
you can use magic.

166
00:09:08,470 --> 00:09:09,760
[Coco exclaims softly]

167
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:20,640
Ever since, it's been my dream
to become a witch,

168
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:22,310
and I can't seem to let it go.

169
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:24,940
I'd be interested in hearing
a bit more about the...

170
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,070
[loud thud]

171
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,820
-[WOMAN 3] Oh, my...
-[WOMAN 2] What was that?

172
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:29,900
[COCO'S MOM] Coco?

173
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,700
-[MAN] Whoa there, settle down.
-[horses neighing]

174
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:35,450
Steady. Steady!

175
00:09:37,490 --> 00:09:39,200
[all gasp]

176
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:41,710
[cattle bleating]

177
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,790
Great, now look what you did.

178
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,460
[TANERL] Shut up. Ow...

179
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:49,710
[COCO] Are you all right?

180
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,340
-Coco.
-[COCO] What happened?

181
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,090
We didn't do anything.
It just suddenly fell apart.

182
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,260
No, it didn't, liar!

183
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:57,430
It fell because you crawled
underneath it!

184
00:09:57,470 --> 00:09:58,600
[TANERL] You snitch!

185
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,100
He hit his head
while he was down there.

186
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,270
And it fell over.

187
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,310
[WOMAN 3]
No! This is absolutely terrible!

188
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:04,770
-[gasping]
-What have you done

189
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:05,900
to our Pegasus Carriage?

190
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,190
[WOMAN 2]
It belongs to my father!

191
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:09,530
We are so sorry!

192
00:10:09,570 --> 00:10:11,900
I'm sure these boys feel awful
for troubling you.

193
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,910
How does your apology help us?

194
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:16,320
Without a carriage,
we can't return home!

195
00:10:16,370 --> 00:10:18,240
[COCO'S MOM]
Oh, dear me, what can we do?

196
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,410
[QIFREY] Pardon me.

197
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:24,170
Perhaps I could be of service.

198
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:26,460
I took a look,

199
00:10:26,590 --> 00:10:28,840
and the damage doesn't appear
to be serious.

200
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:31,050
Really? And who are you?

201
00:10:31,090 --> 00:10:35,140
Apologies, allow me
to cap off my attire.

202
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,680
[Coco gasps]

203
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:40,850
[gasps]

204
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:44,520
Qifrey the witch,
at your service, madam.

205
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:49,570
[BOTH] A pointed hat.

206
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:50,940
You can fix it, then?

207
00:10:51,230 --> 00:10:52,400
[QIFREY] Indeed.

208
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:54,700
[MAN] You certainly are
a lifesaver, Sir Witch!

209
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:55,910
[QIFREY]
It's nothing at all.

210
00:10:55,990 --> 00:10:57,910
Why, I'll simply need to reapply
the spell

211
00:10:57,950 --> 00:10:59,240
to the floorboard
of the carriage.

212
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,450
Your help is appreciated!

213
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,200
And happily given!

214
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:05,170
However, this work
environment is a bit...

215
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:06,500
You can use our workshop,
we would be

216
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,170
-so honored and delighted!
-Coco!

217
00:11:08,210 --> 00:11:10,550
What? We would, Mom,
wouldn't we?

218
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:16,130
I mean, he's an honest
to goodness witch.

219
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,970
This could be the chance
I've been waiting for,

220
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:23,890
to witness the very moment
a spell is cast!

221
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,560
[cattle bleating]

222
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,240
May I ask for your assistance?

223
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,240
I will need someone
to keep watch,

224
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,990
so I can cast
the spell in private.

225
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:41,370
No one must come in
under any circumstances.

226
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:42,620
Thank you.

227
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,670
Guess it was too much
to hope for.

228
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:51,630
Still, why can't we see
how it's done?

229
00:11:52,550 --> 00:11:55,670
Magic is practiced
all over the world,

230
00:11:55,710 --> 00:11:58,970
yet most of us don't have
the first clue how it happens.

231
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:01,850
Only witches know the secret.

232
00:12:02,310 --> 00:12:04,350
The secret... Oh?

233
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:12,940
-[COCO] Where'd they go?
-[TANERL] Almost fell!

234
00:12:13,610 --> 00:12:16,440
[gasps] What do you two think
you're doing?

235
00:12:16,490 --> 00:12:17,490
[KAMLA] She caught us!

236
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:19,110
[TANERL] She doesn't matter.
We're fine.

237
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,410
Can we see into the room
from here?

238
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,910
-[COCO] Wait for me!
-Fine, but keep your voice down!

239
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:26,500
[COCO] Out of the way!

240
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:35,590
[all exclaim]

241
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,970
Man, talk about disappointing.

242
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,470
What a letdown.

243
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,180
[wind howling]

244
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:51,400
[Coco whimpers] What is this?

245
00:12:52,190 --> 00:12:53,400
[Coco gasps]

246
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,610
[wind howling]

247
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:18,920
[Coco gasps]

248
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:23,760
[COCO] I shouldn't!

249
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:27,060
But I really want to!
But I shouldn't!

250
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,190
[gasps softly]

251
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,700
♪

252
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:52,170
[Coco gasps softly]

253
00:13:54,830 --> 00:13:56,420
[COCO] He's drawing.

254
00:14:00,550 --> 00:14:02,630
Drawing magic?

255
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:04,140
With a pen?

256
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:07,220
The wand that I got that day.

257
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,350
Was it actually...

258
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,730
I see now.

259
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:16,230
Witches don't cast spells.

260
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:18,020
They draw them!

261
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:20,990
[QIFREY] That's that.

262
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:23,320
Coco, all finished here.

263
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,870
[Coco panting]

264
00:14:31,410 --> 00:14:32,540
Coco?

265
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:35,710
[COCO] Oh, are you done?
[panting]

266
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:39,090
[horses neighing]

267
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:46,430
[bird squawking]

268
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:51,770
[Coco's mom sighs]

269
00:14:51,810 --> 00:14:54,390
You know, I was starting
to worry there for a moment.

270
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,440
[COCO] Uh?

271
00:14:55,810 --> 00:14:58,230
[COCO'S MOM]
Well, you're in love with magic.

272
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:01,070
You have been ever since
you were little.

273
00:15:01,110 --> 00:15:03,110
So I thought you might ask
to leave home

274
00:15:03,150 --> 00:15:05,200
-and go off with that witch.
-[Coco gasps]

275
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,410
[COCO'S MOM] I already lost
your father to illness.

276
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:11,240
If I had to face
losing you too,

277
00:15:11,290 --> 00:15:12,910
I don't know what I'd do.

278
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:14,460
You never will, Mom!

279
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,880
I promise I won't ever
leave you all alone!

280
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:23,090
[COCO'S MOM] My goodness,
aren't you a sweet girl.

281
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,260
Thank you.

282
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,600
[COCO'S MOM] Hm?

283
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,390
-Mm... [chuckles]
-[giggles]

284
00:15:37,690 --> 00:15:39,020
[both sigh]

285
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,440
Goodnight, Mom.

286
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,150
[COCO'S MOM] Goodnight, dear.

287
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:47,280
-Oh, Coco?
-Hm?

288
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,950
Never mind.

289
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:52,160
Sweet dreams.

290
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,290
You too.

291
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,590
[Coco sighs softly]

292
00:16:02,630 --> 00:16:04,420
I thought you might ask
to leave home

293
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:05,840
and go off with that witch.

294
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,300
[Coco sighs]

295
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:26,320
[COCO] The patterns
in the picture book,

296
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,490
the free wand
that came with it...

297
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:33,330
They were more than
they seemed.

298
00:16:33,370 --> 00:16:35,750
This is a magic pen!

299
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:40,670
[creaking]

300
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:49,590
[COCO] Forgive me, Mom.

301
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:51,550
I won't go anywhere, but...

302
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:54,180
I have to try it!

303
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:15,370
[pen scratching]

304
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:25,420
♪

305
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:39,140
[Coco breathes shakily]

306
00:17:41,350 --> 00:17:43,150
[soft jingling]

307
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:44,440
[COCO] Huh?

308
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:49,150
[groans] Nothing happened.

309
00:17:49,190 --> 00:17:50,740
Now that I think about it,

310
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:52,990
of course it wouldn't be
that easy.

311
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,410
♪

312
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,420
[Coco gasps]

313
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:09,880
[exclaims]

314
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:12,430
[gasps]

315
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:14,760
[exclaims]

316
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:21,390
[COCO] It sparkled!
That must mean it worked!

317
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,060
I can't believe it!
I used magic!

318
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:26,560
I used actual,
real-life magic! [squealing]

319
00:18:26,610 --> 00:18:28,110
So magic is drawn.

320
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:29,570
But I wasn't supposed
to see it!

321
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,240
Will I get into trouble
if he finds out?

322
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:38,580
Maybe I'll draw...

323
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:41,040
just one more.

324
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:42,370
♪

325
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:56,970
[QIFREY] A picture book.
How curious.

326
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,970
Why does it nag at me so?

327
00:19:01,810 --> 00:19:04,480
[gasps] Could it be?

328
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,690
[Coco gasps] A fire spell!

329
00:19:07,730 --> 00:19:09,860
Please stop burning,
please stop burning!

330
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:13,490
[sighs] That was too close.

331
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:15,740
And yet...

332
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:19,700
I think I'm starting
to get the hang of it.

333
00:19:20,330 --> 00:19:23,410
Bigger ones are more powerful
than smaller ones.

334
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:27,130
And neatly drawn ones
last longer than sloppy ones.

335
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:31,000
But drawing them that big
and that neat isn't easy.

336
00:19:31,050 --> 00:19:34,050
Although he certainly
made it look that way.

337
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:35,300
I know!

338
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:36,550
♪

339
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:41,560
[COCO] I was right.

340
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,060
It's a lot easier to be neat

341
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:45,520
when I trace the drawing
rather than copy it.

342
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:56,320
And done!

343
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:58,110
[Coco gasps]

344
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:01,580
♪

345
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:16,550
[Coco gasps]

346
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,970
[QIFREY] What did you draw?

347
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:19,510
Tell me, Coco!

348
00:20:19,550 --> 00:20:21,100
What spell did you draw?

349
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:22,720
I... I don't know.

350
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,810
I traced a pattern
from the book, and I...

351
00:20:24,850 --> 00:20:26,180
-[COCO'S MOM] Coco?
-[Coco gasps]

352
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:28,440
[gasps]

353
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,600
[COCO] Mom?

354
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:35,530
Coco!

355
00:20:35,570 --> 00:20:37,440
Mom, run!

356
00:20:37,490 --> 00:20:39,780
[Coco's mom gasps, screams]

357
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:44,790
No, this isn't real.

358
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:46,790
[cries] Mom!

359
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:48,160
Mom!

360
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:50,960
-Mom! Mom!
-[QIFREY] Forbidden magic!

361
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,420
-Let go! I have to save my mom!
-Hold still!

362
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,760
-She's in danger because of me!
-I don't want to drop you!

363
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,840
[QIFREY] Stop it!

364
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:59,800
That spell is evil,
you mustn't... No!

365
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,310
-[Coco cries]
-[QIFREY] Coco!

366
00:21:06,350 --> 00:21:08,480
[COCO] I'm here, Mom!

367
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,850
[wails] No!

368
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,860
♪

369
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:16,860
[cries] I'm sorry.

370
00:21:17,690 --> 00:21:19,110
I didn't know.

371
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,360
[QIFREY] Of course you didn't.

372
00:21:21,410 --> 00:21:24,580
It was all kept a secret
to prevent tragedies like this.

373
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,960
A special ink,
and a set of Casting Seals.

374
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,870
That's all one needs
for magic to be used.

375
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:34,630
Concealing that is
our One Great Rule.

376
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:37,050
And now that
you know the truth,

377
00:21:37,090 --> 00:21:39,840
you must have
your memories erased.

378
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:42,180
[Coco gasps, cries]

379
00:21:43,050 --> 00:21:45,970
Please don't! I can't forget.

380
00:21:46,010 --> 00:21:47,970
If I do, then who'll save
my mom?

381
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:50,430
I'm afraid I couldn't say.

382
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:53,060
I don't know
what kind of magic it was,

383
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,940
but I can remember
all those drawings by heart!

384
00:21:55,980 --> 00:21:59,070
And if all those memories
are lost, then my mom...

385
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:01,110
[Qifrey gasps] The picture book.

386
00:22:01,490 --> 00:22:02,820
That's right.

387
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,950
If it came
from who I think it did,

388
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,790
then I finally have a link
to their whereabouts!

389
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:09,950
This girl's memories
are my only chance

390
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,790
to track them down!

391
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:14,130
You say you remember
the book by heart?

392
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:15,380
[COCO] Hm.

393
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:17,670
[QIFREY] And you recall
the page you copied?

394
00:22:17,710 --> 00:22:18,880
[COCO] Hmm.

395
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:22,510
[gasps] If we had
the book I used,

396
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:25,340
I could show you
which seal I drew.

397
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:28,890
If we can find the one
that hurt my Mom,

398
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:31,310
do you think there's something
you could do for her?

399
00:22:33,890 --> 00:22:36,690
[QIFREY] There is a chance.

400
00:22:37,900 --> 00:22:41,650
[Coco cries] Mr. Qifrey,
please don't erase my memories!

401
00:22:41,690 --> 00:22:45,660
I'm willing to do anything
to rescue my mother!

402
00:22:47,410 --> 00:22:49,240
Will you keep our secret?

403
00:22:49,290 --> 00:22:50,910
[COCO] I promise!

404
00:22:51,950 --> 00:22:53,710
And are you willing to learn?

405
00:22:53,750 --> 00:22:55,750
To learn... [gasps]

406
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:59,170
[QIFREY] Once you know
the truth, it cannot be undone.

407
00:22:59,210 --> 00:23:02,760
And so, you must join
those trusted with the secret.

408
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:06,840
That is your way forward,
the only way.

409
00:23:08,350 --> 00:23:11,890
-Coco, from now on...
-[gasps]

410
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:15,020
You will be a witch.

411
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:39,880
EPISODE 2:
THE SCHOOL OF THE GRASSLAND

